-- title:
--   Unipotent line through an integral point: adelic lift equals a slash of h
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $h$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let $\Phi\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q})\to\mathbb C$ satisfy [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOfGamma1 h Φ`](def/CuspForm_AdelicLiftGamma1.html#L14), that is: $\Phi(\gamma x)=\Phi(x)$ for every $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)$ mapped into the adelic group by `globalPoints`; $\Phi(xu)=\Phi(x)$ for every $u$ in [`NumberField.AdelicLevel.finiteLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ (AdelicDock.ratLevel M)`](def/NumberField_AdelicLevel.html#L418) pushed forward by [`AdelicDock.finEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145), where `ratLevel M` is the ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ generated by $M$; and $\Phi(g)=\bigl(h\mid_2 \mathrm{ratArchGL2}\,g\bigr)(i)$ for every adelic $g$ with finite component `glFin` equal to $1$ and with [`LanglandsTunnell.ratArchGL2 g`](def/LanglandsTunnell_DeltaLift.html#L16) of positive determinant, where `ratArchGL2` reads off the component of `glArch g` at the default infinite place of $\mathbb Q$ and transports it to $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$ along the isomorphism of that real completion with $\mathbb R$. Let $x=(x_\infty,x_f)$ be an adele of $\mathbb Q$ whose finite part satisfies $x_f{}_v\in\mathcal O_v$ at every finite place. Let $h_1,q$ be adelic matrices with `glFin h₁ = 1`, with $\mathrm{ratArchGL2}\,h_1$ of positive determinant, with `glArch q = 1`, and with `glFin q` in the subgroup `finiteIntegralGL2 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ` (the level-zero subgroup at the unit ideal). Writing $n(y)$ for the upper unipotent matrix `unipotentGL2 y`, the assertion is that there exists $\rho\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$, independent of $t$, such that for every $t\in\mathbb R$,
--   $$\Phi\bigl(n\bigl((x_\infty+\mathrm{ratArchLine}\,t,\;x_f)\bigr)\,h_1\,q\bigr)=\Bigl(h\mid_2\bigl(\rho^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{ratArchGL2}\bigl(n\bigl((x_\infty+\mathrm{ratArchLine}\,t,\;x_f)\bigr)h_1\bigr)\bigr)\Bigr)(i),$$
--   where `ratArchLine t` is the infinite adele all of whose components are $t$ and $\rho$ is viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$.
--
--   This is the classical–adelic dictionary in the form needed along a horizontal line: the values of the adelic lift on the unipotent orbit through an adelically integral point are given by a single slash of the classical weight-two form, by a matrix $\rho\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ that depends on the finite data only. It is used in the verification that the lift of a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ is cuspidal, [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOfGamma1.isCuspidalFn_productionPinsGeneral`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOfGamma1.isCuspidalFn_productionPinsGeneral), where the constant term is computed by integrating over $t$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_IsAdelicLiftOfGamma1_exists_forall_apply_unipotentGL2_add_ratArchLine_mul_eq_slash_apply_I.lean

